  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday) \nIssued at 1033 PM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nUneventful weather still looks to pan out through the rest of the \nweek as dry northwest flow aloft persists over our region. There is \nstill a few questions regarding temperatures due to uncertainty in \nhow a secondary upper low off the CA coast evolves, but model \nconsensus favors neutral or slightly positive midlevel height \ntendencies as this feature likely tracks well to our south. Surface \nridging is expected to remain in place over the central CONUS during \nthis period, but a return to a predominantly southerly surface \nwind locally should allow for a modest warmup across West TX \nWednesday into the upcoming weekend. Precipitation chances remain \nlow through the extended period with the polar jet stream \nremaining to our north.",
